trace.request:
Please perform and report findings of:  
- Log roll test: gently rotate the right hip internally and externally while the patient is supine and knee is flexed to 90° — note location and severity of pain;  
- FABER test: flex right hip and knee to 90°, then abduct and externally rotate the hip (foot placed on opposite knee) — note pain location (anterior groin vs posterior SI joint) and reproduction of symptoms.

